{"path":"s23","heading":"Statements of claim and defence.","in_1996":true,"nodes_1996":[{"path":"s23","node_type":"section","number":"23","heading":"Statements of claim and defence.","text":""},{"path":"s23.ss1","node_type":"subsection","number":"1","heading":null,"text":"Within the period of time agreed upon by the parties or determined by the arbitral tribunal, the claimant shall state the facts supporting his claim, the points at issue and the relief or remedy sought, and the respondent shall state his defence in respect of these particulars, unless the parties have otherwise agreed as to the required elements of those statements."},{"path":"s23.ss2","node_type":"subsection","number":"2","heading":null,"text":"The parties may submit with their statements all documents they consider to be relevant or may add a reference to the documents or other evidence they will submit."},{"path":"s23.ss3","node_type":"subsection","number":"3","heading":null,"text":"Unless otherwise agreed by the parties, either party may amend or supplement his claim or defence during the course of the arbitral proceedings, unless the arbitral tribunal considers it inappropriate to allow the amendment or supplement having regard to the delay in making it."}],"events":[{"instrument":"3/2016","title":"Arbitration and Conciliation (Amendment) Act, 2015 (No. 3 of 2016)","effective":"from 23 Oct 2015 (Ordinance 9 of 2015)","edges":[{"instrument":"3/2016","old":null,"new":"s23.ss2A","op_type":"insert","source":"rule","group":"3/2016|s11","confidence":1.0,"rationale":null}],"instructions":{"3/2016|s11":"In section 23 of the principal Act, after sub-section (2), the following sub-section shall be inserted, namely:— “(2A) The respondent, in support of his case, may also submit a counterclaim or plead a set-off, which shall be adjudicated upon by the arbitral tribunal, if such counterclaim or set-off falls within the scope of the arbitration agreement.”."},"intent":[{"unit":"3/2016|s11","status":"not_determinable","claim":"intent not determinable from available record","tier":null,"quote":null,"document_id":null,"span":null,"attribution":null,"tiers_searched":["sor","debate","report"]}]},{"instrument":"33/2019","title":"Arbitration and Conciliation (Amendment) Act, 2019 (No. 33 of 2019)","effective":"in part: ss. 1, 4–9, 11–13, 15 from 30 Aug 2019 (S.O. 3154(E)); other sections by later notification or not commenced","edges":[{"instrument":"33/2019","old":null,"new":"s23.ss4","op_type":"insert","source":"rule","group":"33/2019|s5","confidence":1.0,"rationale":null}],"instructions":{"33/2019|s5":"In section 23 of the principal Act, after sub-section (3), the following sub-section shall be inserted, namely:— “(4) The statement of claim and defence under this section shall be completed within a period of six months from the date the arbitrator or all the arbitrators, as the case may be, received notice, in writing, of their appointment.”."},"intent":[{"unit":"33/2019|s5","status":"sourced","claim":"The amendment is intended to ensure that the statement of claim and defence is completed within six months of the arbitrator’s appointment.","tier":"sor","quote":"(iv) to amend section 23 of the Act relating to \"Statement of claim and defence\"\nso as to provide that the statement of claim and defence shall be completed within a\nperiod of six months from the date the arbitrator receives the notice of appointment;","document_id":28,"span":[27930,28181],"attribution":{"by":"Government","role":"government","where":"Statement of Objects and Reasons, The Arbitration and Conciliation (Amendment) Bill, 2019 (as introduced in Rajya Sabha)","signed_by":"RAVI SHANKAR PRASAD"},"tiers_searched":["sor"]}]}]}